he denominator is BARMER-only.","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/presse/hib/kurzmeldungen-1140288","date":"2026-01-29","source_name":"Deutscher Bundestag hib 76/2026; Drucksache 21/3873","source_type":"press","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Adds a German political and regulatory risk to NIPT volume that is not in the known list, which covers only US/ACMG items."},{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"German NIPT uptake of ~50% leaves headroom, and the age curves are still drifting up, so volume growth is not over.","detail":"BARMER Q1 2024 data (Ärzteblatt Int. 2025) show 482 NIPTs per 1,000 pregnancies, with 784 per 1,000 receiving counseling, and 302 of the counseled (38%) had no NIPT. The factsheet says uptake in under-26s rose to ~25-30% and reached ~80% in the over-40s by 2025. Counseling reach of 50-75% by age and the 38% counseled-but-untested pool suggest further room. A monitoring rule or false-positive concerns could still slow it.","url":"https://di.aerzteblatt.de/int/archive/article/244021","date":"2025-03","source_name":"Deutsches Ärzteblatt International (Hertle & Wende)","source_type":"claims_data","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Quantifies German headroom (482 per 1,000 in Q1 2024) with a denominator, unlike the known list."}],"new_candidates":[{"url":"https://www.bifg.de/media/dl/Journals/gynaekologische_praxis_2026.pdf","why":"Table 2 with quarterly service frequencies, which would give the numeric quarterly series."},{"url":"https://www.lobbyregister.bundestag.de/media/b3/bd/707537/Stellungnahme-Gutachten-SG2603180008.pdf","why":"Lobbyregister statement citing ~48% uptake for 2022-2024 pregnancies and possibly national numbers."},{"url":"https://dserver.bundestag.de/btd/21/060/2106075.pdf","why":"Follow-up Bundestag document that surfaced in the search; possibly a government answer with national NIPT counts."}],"apify_requests":[]}
